# This repo is authored on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but every script runs on
# a Linux SLURM cluster. Without these rules a fresh clone gets CRLF shell
# scripts, and bash fails with `$'\r': command not found` on the shebang line -
# a confusing failure that looks like a cluster problem rather than a checkout
# problem. Force LF for everything that is executed or parsed remotely.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Keyword tier files are read line-by-line by the filters; a trailing \r would
# be folded into the keyword itself and silently match nothing.
*.txt  text eol=lf

# Data files: newline-delimited JSON is parsed line-by-line on Linux.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
